<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Status bar notification icon.

  Deliberately a plain filled shape, not a copy of the launcher icon: Android renders this at a
  small size, silhouette-only, and re-tints it to white (or the channel's colour) regardless of
  what colour is drawn here - a detailed or multi-colour icon just turns into an illegible blob.
  A bell is the standard Android notification glyph, so it reads at a glance as "you have a
  notification" the same way every other app's icon does, rather than needing to be puzzled out.
-->
